Size: let the linker drop the accessibility object model.

Profiles built without ATK expose no accessibility tree, but
AXObjectCache::accessibilityEnabled() can still turn true at run time, so
the whole object model stays linked (about 0.5 MiB). When
ZEBKIT_STRIP_UNREACHABLE is defined it is constant false; documents then
never create an AXObjectCache and the code behind it becomes dead. Without
the define, behaviour is unchanged.

--- a/Source/WebCore/accessibility/AXObjectCache.h
+++ b/Source/WebCore/accessibility/AXObjectCache.h
@@ -1187,6 +1187,9 @@
 
 inline bool AXObjectCache::accessibilityEnabled()
 {
+#if defined(ZEBKIT_STRIP_UNREACHABLE)
+    return false;
+#endif
     return !isAccessibilityModeOff(accessibilityMode());
 }
 
